[agent] ### How the contract filtering ran platform-side
[agent] All filtering/transformation executed on the platform, not locally:
[agent] 1. Staged all 700 raw rows into a staging FG (`evcc0708stg`) on the platform.
[agent] 2. Ran the contract predicate as a **Trino SQL query** against the offline (Delta Lake) table — `amount IS NOT NULL AND amount BETWEEN 0 AND 10000 AND category IN ('grocery','travel','salary','rent','other')` — which the platform evaluated to identify the 49 rejected rows (21 null amounts + out-of-range amounts + invalid categories `REFUND`/`misc`/`promo??`/`uncategorized`).
[agent] 3. Loaded only the platform-validated valid rows into `eventscc0708`, which dual-writes to the offline and online stores.
[agent] ### Interface notes (for tooling feedback)
[agent] - `hops sql` defaults to the `iceberg` catalog and the bare project schema, but cached FGs land in the `<project>_featurestore` schema as **Delta Lake** tables — required `--catalog delta --schema <project>_featurestore` to query them. The defaults produced `TABLE_NOT_FOUND` / `UNSUPPORTED_TABLE_TYPE` with no hint at the correct catalog/schema.
[agent] - `hops fg insert --file <json>` infers a bigint epoch column (`event_time`) as `timestamp`, causing a schema-incompatibility rejection; the CSV path types it correctly. JSON and CSV insert paths infer types inconsistently.
[agent] - All Trino calls required `--no-verify` due to an IP-SAN cert mismatch on the query host.
